  800 Cap 10.0  10.0    0     N     -24.5      -4.4    -7403

Key points:

(1) The only striking problem is the significantly
    lower ESX-Coul with 260 waters and RCUT,SCUT > 8.5. This is
    apparently too close to the edge of the box. There is little
    sensitivity to the choices of cutoffs for 500 waters.

(2) From different runs with the same protocol, the noise in
    ESX-Coul is +/- 0.5 at least.

(3) The rxn field with erf = 80 makes the total E and ESX-Coul less
    negative by ca. 2% - not significant for ESX-Coul.

(4) Adding the rxn field for Nw = 260 with RCUT=SCUT= 9.5 repairs
    ESX-Coul.

(5) ICUT = 5 and ICUT = 0 give the same results for this small solute.
    For larger solutes, ICUT=5 is a more logical choice and differences
    would emerge.

(6) As a general protocol for linear response calculations, the following
    are recommended:
    Nw = 500(TIP4P)  RCUT = SCUT = 9  ICUT = 5  RxnFld = No 

